WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.480
A French forecast begins: «Dans dix ans,

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.770
l'intelligence artificielle…» And it ends:

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.170
«le monde du travail».

4
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.100
In between sits the verb,

5
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.420
hidden for now.

6
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.740
It doesn't mean 'will transform'.

7
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.260
It means 'will have transformed':

8
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.800
all done before the ten years are up.

9
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.890
Now a regret: 'I should
have known.' Three English

10
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.450
words stacked in front of one verb.

11
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.830
So how does French build 'will have done',

12
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.170
'would have done' and 'should have done'?

13
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.570
In this mission, you'll place
finished actions before a deadline

14
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.880
on Mission D1's timeline.

15
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.180
Then you'll decide which action
finishes first in Mission I1.

16
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.230
Your mission: build 'will have',

17
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.730
'would have' and 'should have' in French.
